@jrouwe I'm finding myself asking sort of the same question that I asked you [here](https://github.com/godot-jolt/godot-jolt/issues/984#issuecomment-2368081772), which is that I don't really know what this value should be now, seeing as how it's no longer based on anything like `JPH::QuadTree::cStackSize`, but instead based on what I assume is this:

https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/1bbfe637c62d48dd455562bf2bc24d92e6ba9ade/thirdparty/jolt_physics/Jolt/Physics/Collision/BroadPhase/BroadPhaseQuadTree.cpp#L39-L43

Should we be trying to replicate that calculation in some way, based on the `physics/jolt_physics_3d/limits/max_bodies` project setting, or is this low enough of a value to be reasonable across the board?
